<title>ITALY: Mediobanca rises on Olivetti talk.</title>
<headline>Mediobanca rises on Olivetti talk.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Italy's leading merchant banks Mediobanca rose on the Milan bourse on market talk that the secretive deal-making bank would not come to the rescue of trouble information technology group Olivetti.</p>
<p>Dealers said that there was talk that Mediobanca would not attempt a costly rescue of Olivetti, which showed mounting problems this week as it released half-year 1996 results which showed slumping sales, rising debt and continuing losses.</p>
<p>Mediobanca shares rose 2.54 percent to 8,100 lire in a generally firmer Milan bourse, with Olivetti shares suspended pending a statement on its financial accounts after its meeting with stock market authority Consob on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
